Chapter: ProbeClosureArity2Sat

 Positive control at arity 2. `make2` takes two parameters and returns a
 function. `sat2` names it with BOTH -- a complete call -- and is never
 called itself. The driver exercises only make2.

 A fault reproduces the saturated-naming effect at an arity other than 1,
 and pairs with probe-closure-arity2-unsat, which names the same
 definition incompletely.

Section: Shapes

  add4 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add4 (w) (x) (y) (z) = w + x + y + z

  make2 : Integer, Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make2 (a) (b) = (add4 a) b

 Names make2 with 2 of its 2 parameters. Defined, never called.

  sat2 : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  sat2 (n) = (make2 n) n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("sat 53 expected: " & show ((((make2 5) 6) 20) 22))
  end
